{
  "schema": 1,
  "title": "How a plugin becomes one score",
  "mechanism": "The model grades each judgment check with a quote; the script folds every grade into six weighted dimensions, one composite, and a verdict.",
  "lens": "transformation",
  "claim": "Every number on the scorecard is the script's: the model's only say is a 0-4 grade it has to back with a quote.",
  "implication": "Two runs that agree on the grades agree on the score, and fix_deltas, not intuition, says which fix buys the most.",
